00:15:42.730 --> 00:15:47.030
Oh, that's a separate card called low pony, question mark.

330
00:15:47.350 --> 00:15:47.830
Okay.

331
00:15:48.210 --> 00:15:49.470
Where should we start?

332
00:15:49.610 --> 00:15:52.070
Should we start with what or low pony?

333
00:15:52.330 --> 00:15:54.890
Let's start with what and then go into low pony.

334
00:15:55.370 --> 00:15:55.670
Great.

335
00:15:56.050 --> 00:16:01.490
Pam calls Kevin Kev and then Buddy and they fist bump.

336
00:16:01.670 --> 00:16:02.610
What is happening?

337
00:16:03.090 --> 00:16:04.270
What is happening?

338
00:16:04.270 --> 00:16:07.470
The fist bump was a reluctant fist bump though, Ange.

339
00:16:07.630 --> 00:16:09.830
I know, but Kev, Buddy, fist bump.

340
00:16:09.830 --> 00:16:10.330
She's being condescending.

341
00:16:10.650 --> 00:16:12.310
She's being totally condescending.

342
00:16:12.550 --> 00:16:13.710
She's trying to put him off.

343
00:16:13.890 --> 00:16:17.950
She's like, Kev, Buddy, fist bump, leave my desk.

344
00:16:18.210 --> 00:16:20.610
I mean, she's trying to get through it.

345
00:16:20.710 --> 00:16:21.930
That's my interpretation.

346
00:16:22.550 --> 00:16:25.850
My interpretation was that he's like a little kid.

347
00:16:26.250 --> 00:16:26.610
Yeah.

348
00:16:26.890 --> 00:16:27.250
Yeah.

349
00:16:27.510 --> 00:16:28.430
So she's like, okay, Kev.

350
00:16:28.450 --> 00:16:30.630
She's patronizing him for sure.

351
00:16:30.630 --> 00:16:37.170
But you just don't often hear Pam sort of become that casual with Kevin.

352
00:16:37.430 --> 00:16:41.070
Or, you know, I feel like she saves that part of herself for Jim and everyone else.

353
00:16:41.170 --> 00:16:44.290
She's sort of just aloof to a little bit.

354
00:16:44.450 --> 00:16:46.510
So it just kind of was startling to me.

355
00:16:46.710 --> 00:16:47.870
That and your low ponytail.

356
00:16:48.290 --> 00:16:49.190
I mean, what the heck?

357
00:16:49.950 --> 00:16:51.630
Here's the deal with the low pony.

358
00:16:52.030 --> 00:16:53.790
I think it was a swing and a miss.

359
00:16:55.130 --> 00:16:57.730
I wasn't crazy about it when I saw it.

360
00:16:57.730 --> 00:17:00.690
But we were trying to change things up.

361
00:17:00.790 --> 00:17:07.830
You might notice as well, Pam has got a little bit of like a pinkier, sparklier eyeshadow on in this episode as well.

362
00:17:07.970 --> 00:17:08.870
And a little lip gloss.

363
00:17:09.050 --> 00:17:09.810
There's so much pink.

364
00:17:09.950 --> 00:17:12.910
She has pink eyeshadow, pink lipstick, pink sweater.

365
00:17:13.210 --> 00:17:16.150
But then the low pony with the clip.

366
00:17:16.530 --> 00:17:18.110
Not even a ponytail holder.

367
00:17:18.410 --> 00:17:19.390
I can't wait.

368
00:17:19.550 --> 00:17:19.650
Wait.

369
00:17:19.650 --> 00:17:20.570
I sounded so Southern.

370
00:17:20.790 --> 00:17:21.750
It's very hard for me.

371
00:17:22.110 --> 00:17:22.590
Holder.

372
00:17:22.770 --> 00:17:26.350
Anyway, it's a clip holding your hair, not even a ponytail holder.

373
00:17:26.350 --> 00:17:29.610
Yeah, well, the clip is humongous.

374
00:17:29.990 --> 00:17:30.990
Here's the thing.

375
00:17:31.230 --> 00:17:41.710
The conversation in hair and makeup was that Pam would be experimenting a little bit because she's going to her art classes.

376
00:17:41.850 --> 00:17:43.450
She's living on her own.

377
00:17:43.450 --> 00:17:54.830
We needed to see some physical representation of the fact that she's attempting, even in small ways, to break out of her shell right now, to break out of her routines.

378
00:17:55.630 --> 00:17:57.230
So there you go.

379
00:17:57.230 --> 00:17:59.010
We offer the low pony.

380
00:17:59.730 --> 00:18:05.870
I'm going to say I think you never see it again because it wasn't great.

381
00:18:06.170 --> 00:18:07.990
Can we just say it wasn't great?

382
00:18:08.110 --> 00:18:09.430
It's a clip low pony.

383
00:18:09.970 --> 00:18:10.530
Yeah.

384
00:18:10.830 --> 00:18:11.430
A clip low pony.

385
00:18:11.430 --> 00:18:14.150
Now, I kind of wish they'd really gone for it.

386
00:18:14.230 --> 00:18:15.870
Next week, you would have had a banana clip.

387
00:18:16.050 --> 00:18:16.890
Remember those things?

388
00:18:17.150 --> 00:18:17.430
Oh, God.

389
00:18:17.490 --> 00:18:18.890
They gave you like a mohawk.

390
00:18:19.750 --> 00:18:20.190
Yeah.

391
00:18:20.490 --> 00:18:20.730
Yeah.

392
00:18:21.190 --> 00:18:21.770
All right.

393
00:18:21.890 --> 00:18:23.910
Well, it was a moment in time.

394
00:18:24.290 --> 00:18:25.590
It was something we tried.

395
00:18:26.550 --> 00:18:29.850
Unfortunately, it's there for us all to see again and again.

396
00:18:30.130 --> 00:18:30.310
Okay.

397
00:18:30.450 --> 00:18:32.110
Don't say unfortunately to me.

398
00:18:32.250 --> 00:18:34.530
Do you see how many low ponies my character has?

399
00:18:34.690 --> 00:18:36.350
Like all the crazy hair views I have.

400
00:18:36.350 --> 00:18:38.130
Listen, I don't have a problem with a low pony.

401
00:18:38.290 --> 00:18:40.290
I don't have a problem with a low pony in general.

402
00:18:40.290 --> 00:18:46.910
I'm just saying this particular low pony was, because of the giant clip, it was odd.

403
00:18:47.950 --> 00:18:49.790
We're back in Michael's office.

404
00:18:50.450 --> 00:18:53.310
And Jenna, I don't know if you've ever had to fire someone.

