00:20:31.990 --> 00:20:35.290
It's set next to her desk all nine seasons.

439
00:20:35.890 --> 00:20:37.030
And it just sat there.

440
00:20:37.130 --> 00:20:38.850
And sometimes if she had to do background stuff.

441
00:20:38.970 --> 00:20:45.250
But this was a great panning shot because, you know, Michael says there is no Stanley tree and he's napping.

442
00:20:45.690 --> 00:20:49.570
And then they said, do you think the world is crawling with Phyllis's and she's knitting?

443
00:20:49.810 --> 00:20:51.290
So it was this great visual.

444
00:20:51.510 --> 00:20:52.930
But no, Phyllis can't knit.

445
00:20:53.490 --> 00:20:53.670
Yeah.

446
00:20:54.310 --> 00:20:54.790
No.

447
00:20:55.210 --> 00:20:55.690
No.

448
00:20:55.910 --> 00:20:57.950
That's one of my favorite talking heads, though.

449
00:20:58.110 --> 00:20:58.790
I love that one.

450
00:20:59.010 --> 00:20:59.750
I do, too.

451
00:20:59.970 --> 00:21:00.610
I do, too.

452
00:21:01.150 --> 00:21:03.670
So then Michael is walking around the office.

453
00:21:04.610 --> 00:21:07.670
Dwight can tell something's wrong, but Michael isn't spilling.

454
00:21:07.670 --> 00:21:17.150
And this is my other favorite talking head from this episode, which is Dwight's talking head, where he says, when you're close to someone, you can read them like a book.

455
00:21:17.430 --> 00:21:25.110
And he says, Michael's book is titled, Something Weird is Going On, Colon, What Did Jan Say?

456
00:21:25.590 --> 00:21:30.970
The Michael Scott Story by Michael Scott with Dwight Schrute.

457
00:21:31.950 --> 00:21:34.730
All right, that last part is not in the script,

458
00:21:34.730 --> 00:21:43.210
and I could kind of tell that there was an improv there because whenever Rain improvs at the end of a talking head or the end of a scene,

459
00:21:43.530 --> 00:21:48.810
I feel like you can see him smile just a little bit in the corners of his mouth and his eyes.

460
00:21:48.810 --> 00:21:57.110
So I reached out to Mike Schur, and he told me that he and Rain expanded on the book title on the day, on set.

461
00:21:57.290 --> 00:21:58.590
They kept throwing out ideas.

462
00:21:58.870 --> 00:22:03.410
The original was just supposed to be Something Weird is Going On, Colon, What Did Jan Say?

463
00:22:03.590 --> 00:22:09.050
And Mike threw out the Michael Scott story, and then Rain added with Dwight Schrute.

464
00:22:09.450 --> 00:22:10.190
Yeah, for sure.

465
00:22:10.410 --> 00:22:12.330
I mean, I feel like we all have tells.

466
00:22:12.650 --> 00:22:18.450
And Rain, when he has an improv that I think he's really happy with, has a little bit of a smirk.

467
00:22:18.450 --> 00:22:20.210
He's kind of proud of the moment.

468
00:22:20.490 --> 00:22:22.690
He amuses himself in the moment while saying it.

469
00:22:22.910 --> 00:22:32.110
Now things are really getting heightened over at the Stanford branch because Karen breaks the news that the Scranton branch is closing to Jim, and oh my God, Jim's face.

470
00:22:32.110 --> 00:22:33.030
He's like, what?

471
00:22:33.250 --> 00:22:35.450
You notice he doesn't reach out to Pam.

472
00:22:35.630 --> 00:22:39.570
Pam and Jim never call one another or text one another in this whole day.

473
00:22:40.090 --> 00:22:47.910
It's kind of weird because in Diwali, we see that Pam was texting Jim, and they had that phone call.

474
00:22:48.450 --> 00:22:49.670
At the end of grief counseling.

475
00:22:50.350 --> 00:22:51.810
But what's going on?

476
00:22:51.990 --> 00:22:53.090
Why no communication?

477
00:22:53.470 --> 00:22:55.010
It makes perfect sense to me.

478
00:22:55.230 --> 00:22:59.910
You know, they're both sort of struggling with where do we go from here?

479
00:23:00.370 --> 00:23:08.070
And I'm sure Pam's first instinct is to reach out to him, but she doesn't feel like she has that kind of access to him anymore.

480
00:23:08.430 --> 00:23:09.530
She rejected him.

481
00:23:09.530 --> 00:23:12.290
So, no, it makes perfect sense to me that they don't communicate.

482
00:23:12.290 --> 00:23:17.390
What I thought was weirder, and we're going to get to it, is that Roy finds out from accounting.

483
00:23:17.990 --> 00:23:19.730
So Pam didn't even tell Roy.

484
00:23:20.010 --> 00:23:20.650
That's right.

485
00:23:20.950 --> 00:23:24.230
So now Michael approaches Pam at front reception.

486
00:23:24.450 --> 00:23:25.870
He's acting really strange.

487
00:23:26.110 --> 00:23:32.230
She clearly knows something is up because he was moaning in his office, and Jan visited.

488
00:23:32.230 --> 00:23:34.410
So Pam's like, what's going on, Michael?

489
00:23:35.150 --> 00:23:35.870
Yeah.

490
00:23:36.050 --> 00:23:38.250
I have a fan catch from this moment.

